course: dictionary
lesson: 6572
title: Nightfall
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Nightfall is a noun. It means the time in the evening when it becomes dark, also called dusk. The word is made of two smaller words, night and fall, which is a good clue to its meaning.
explain: Toad is cross with himself in the story: «What did I want to go strutting about the country... instead of hiding till nightfall and slipping home quietly by back ways!» The clues are hiding and slipping home quietly. Toad means he should have waited for the dark, so nightfall is the time when it gets dark enough to hide.
explain: Look for the phrases «at nightfall», «before nightfall» and «by nightfall». «We must get home before nightfall» means finish the walk while it is still light. To check, swap in dusk: «We must get home before dusk» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Nightfall means the time in the evening when it becomes dark.
fact: Nightfall is another word for dusk.
fact: Nightfall is an uncountable noun, so we do not say "a nightfall" or "nightfalls".
fact: Useful phrases: «at nightfall», «before nightfall» and «by nightfall».
fact: On a walk, plan to be home or have a torch ready before nightfall.
exercise: «We must get home before nightfall.» What does nightfall mean here? | A loud noise in the woods | The very start of the morning | *The time in the evening when it becomes dark | The middle of the afternoon
exercise: Toad wants to wait «till nightfall». Find and copy one word that means the same as nightfall. | midday | *dusk | sunrise | breakfast
exercise: Complete the safety tip: Plan to be home ___ nightfall. | boring | yellow | sleepy | *before
test: Toad says he should have been «hiding till nightfall» and «slipping home quietly by back ways». What does the story suggest about his plan? | *He wanted to wait until it was dark, so he could sneak home unseen | He wanted to wait until breakfast so he could eat first | He was planning a party at tea-time | He wanted to sing in the sunshine at midday
test: Which phrase means at the time when it becomes dark? | *at nightfall | at tea-time | in the morning | at midday
exam: Jade writes, «The walkers camped by nightfall.» What does by nightfall mean? | Before breakfast the next morning | *Before or when it has become dark | At midday, when the sun is high | Never, because the walkers never stopped
